  {
    "id": 186666,
    "title": "Complete a compilation of written process safety information before conducting any process hazard analysis.",
    "description": "Complete a compilation of written process safety information before conducting any process hazard analysis.\n\n- Compile written process safety information to identify and understand hazards of processes involving highly hazardous chemicals.\n- Include information on the hazards of the chemicals, such as toxicity, permissible exposure limits, physical data, reactivity, corrosivity, stability, and hazardous effects of mixing materials.\n- Include information on the technology of the process, such as flow diagrams, process chemistry, inventory limits, safe operating limits, and consequences of deviations.\n- Include information on the equipment, such as materials of construction, piping and instrument diagrams, electrical classification, relief and ventilation system design, design codes, material and energy balances, and safety systems.\n- Document compliance with recognized engineering practices and ensure safe operation of equipment designed to outdated standards.",
    "type_id": 3,
    "category": 1,
    "priority": 0,
    "recurring_frequency_rule": "YEARLY",
