  {
    "id": 186667,
    "title": "Perform an initial process hazard analysis and update it every five years.",
    "description": "Perform an initial process hazard analysis and update it every five years.\n\n- Conduct an initial process hazard analysis for each process, considering its complexity and potential hazards.\n- Use appropriate methodologies such as What-If, Checklist, HAZOP, FMEA, Fault Tree Analysis, or equivalent.\n- Ensure the analysis addresses process hazards, previous incidents, controls, facility siting, human factors, and potential safety and health effects.\n- Form a team with expertise in engineering and process operations, including at least one employee with specific process knowledge and one knowledgeable in the analysis methodology.\n- Establish a system to address and document the team's findings and recommendations, and communicate actions to affected employees.\n- Retain all analyses and documented resolutions for the life of the process.",
    "type_id": 3,
    "category": 1,
    "priority": 0,
    "recurring_frequency_rule": "YEARLY",
